From 6d5522771539c1d6bcce536aa740c3d9592eaa77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Maxime=20M=C3=A9r=C3=A9?= <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 15:53:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: rng: stm32-rng: add post-init-providers property
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The STM32MP15 SCMI device trees set post-init-providers on the RNG
node to defer clock/reset provider initialization until after the
device has been configured. This property is currently rejected by
the schema since additionalProperties is false and the property was
not declared, e.g.:

  rng@54003000 (st,stm32-rng): 'post-init-providers' does not
  match any of the regexes: '^pinctrl-[0-9]+$'

Declare post-init-providers so dtbs_check no longer flags it.

Change-Id: Ib0b5711e5eccccc89a83cb450051aeb033042838
Signed-off-by: Maxime Méré <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/589195
Reviewed-by: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/rng/st,stm32-rng.yaml | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/rng/st,stm32-rng.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/rng/st,stm32-rng.yaml
@@ -53,6 +53,8 @@ properties:
   power-domains:
     maxItems: 1
 
+  post-init-providers: true
+
 required:
   - compatible
   - reg
